From 46afea3ec7eb400498d3f7b78a735c4db7251941 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: loop-uh <loop-uh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:40:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Accept client sockets handed over by the node's 443
 dispatcher

A unix listen path ending in .handoff is a SOCK_SEQPACKET listener whose
clients are TCP sockets passed with SCM_RIGHTS by the node's 443
dispatcher (vpnbot node-services go/cmd/sni-dispatch). The dispatcher
peeks the ClientHello without consuming it, picks the inbound by SNI and
hands over the client socket itself, so the inbound reads the untouched
ClientHello, sees the real client address and no proxy stays in the data
path. Accept returns *net.TCPConn; anything else received is closed; a
full backlog holds the sender (backpressure); Close ends Accept with
net.ErrClosed and frees the path. acceptProxyProtocol is refused on such a
path: there is no proxy, so there is no header.

Capability marker: vpnbot-socket-handoff-v1.
